1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
This is a bill that I put forward that would lay the framework for America to lead in the area of quantum computing.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:14,000
I mean, we are at the precipice of something huge that's going to transform all the way things operate.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
I mean, AI and quantum computing to follow.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,000
I mean, this is the next level.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,000
And we're in a moon race with the Chinese right now.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Whoever has AI and quantum supremacy will be the world superpower.

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,000
And a lot of the negative information you see out there didn't sprout up by accident.

8
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:39,000
You notice how all the negativity that's just popped out of nowhere all over social media?

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,000
There is a Chinese disinformation campaign coming down in this country and we don't even know it.

10
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
It's being funded because they don't want America to compete.

11
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,000
They want to beat us from within.

12
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,000
But we need a framework in place to make sure we're ready.

13
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:02,000
And that's what the Quantum Computing Act is about because we have to lead and you have to be prepared to lead.

14
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:07,000
So it's in the jurisdiction of my committee, which is the Energy and Commerce Committee.

15
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,000
We've got the broadest jurisdiction on any committee in Congress.

16
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,000
We have all the technology, telecommunications, healthcare, and energy policy.

17
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Only a couple of big things.

18
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,000
They're going to break that up a little bit?

19
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:19,000
It keeps me pretty busy and I get to read a lot.

20
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:28,000
But you also get the most fascinating meetings in the people that come to Washington and I go to them that are really,

21
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:34,000
I mean, just the breakthroughs that we're on the cusp of in terms of medicine, Alzheimer's disease, pancreatic cancer.

22
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:39,000
I mean, a lot of that's being brought to us with the help of AI.

23
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:47,000
You know, when you take 100 million medical data points and run them against each other to try to crack the code and find the solution of what's going to work.

24
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:52,000
It doesn't replace the doctors and the researchers, but it gives them a tool that they've never had.

25
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
And we can save a lot of lives with this.

26
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,000
And to your point, if we're behind the eight ball on this, where does it lead?

27
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,000
It leads to the Chinese being the supremacy in the world.

28
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,000
And we can't afford that.

